WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:07.650
<b>on) I tried making a new song</b>

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.090
<i>Hello! This is Neon!</i>

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.130
<i>Thank you for always listening.</i>

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.960
<i>Today, I hope you'll listen to my new song,</i>

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.320
<i>"Bloom in Many Layers."</i>

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.370
<b>on) I tried making a new song</b>

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.280
<i>Will I be able to say it right?</i>

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.190
<i>Will I be able to tell you?</i>

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:35.030
<i>Honest words would be the best, but...</i>

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:33.760
<b>Get more popular!</b>

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.970
<b>Your mask is so cute</b>

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.180
<b>Liked and subscribed</b>

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.390
<b>I feel healed</b>

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.270
<i>If I wrote it in the sky</i>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.600
<b>Thanks for uploading</b>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.430
<b>It's so easy to listen to</b>

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.430
<b>I want you to get more popular</b>

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.280
<i>Would you smile?</i>

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:51.180
<i>Even though there's nothing good about me</i>

00:00:52.990 --> 00:01:00.910
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:29.540
<b>Echoing Through the Hydrangea</b>

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.610
Mittsu, do you have work again today?

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.670
Hm? Yes.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:37.960
You make your own lunches and you 
help out at home. You're amazing!

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.050
No, this is just what I always do.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.700
Oh, right! Look!

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.180
He's from the place you work at, right?

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.850
Y-Yes.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.050
I heard he played in a band in Tokyo.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.830
Wow! Really?

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.020
Thank you!

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.600
Thank you!

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.770
Make sure they appreciate 
you when they eat you!

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.310
Isn't it about time to get used 
to saying goodbye to the sweets?

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.680
That's right.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:12.840
What will you do once you get the point 
where you can make sweets yourself?

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.840
Nagomu-san, please use this.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.480
Mitsuru-chan...

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.380
It's still brand new.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.090
Thank you.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.170
I'll wash it and return it.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.150
I'm so sorry! They're my little brother's!

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.690
The pattern's similar, 
so I grabbed them by mistake!

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.180
Well... I'm glad they were brand new.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.190
What's wrong?

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:39.240
He's worn them more than a few times.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.360
Let's not say anything.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.280
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.280
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.030
Welcome!

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.570
<b>Oak Leaf Mochi</b>

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.570
<b>Noblewoman's Raiment</b>

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.570
<b>Secret Letter</b>

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.620
Oh, these are cute!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.880
Lovely, aren't they? 
They're original to our shop.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.960
Can we have two matching ones, please?

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.430
Thank you!

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.210
<b>Don't forget to
wash your hands
and mouth!</b>

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.040
I'll help!

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.210
Thanks.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:04.710
Thank you for helping me study the other day.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.470
I got 100 on the test!

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:11.850
Oh! Congratulations! I'm glad I could help!

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.880
Let's do something fun together next time.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:14.730
Yes, let's!

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.070
What are you looking at? You're being creepy.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.590
Excuse me!

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:21.990
Coming!

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:27.880
I was just thinking... Itsuka doesn't
 ever look me in the eye.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:32.220
Well, anyone would hate 
being stared at like that.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.840
Hello.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:43.980
Otsurusan, you're off today, aren't you?

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.590
Hello!

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.590
Hi!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.530
Hello.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:51.100
I thought I'd buy my grandchildren 
something sweet to eat today.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:55.770
I see. Please, come this way. We have
 an open table toward the back.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.440
Is it good?

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.650
Yeah!

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:05.210
Oh! You've got anko on your cheek.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.800
Mitarashi Heaven Bomber!

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:10.490
Koume!

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.990
Young master, I'm so sorry!

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.580
Oh, it's fine.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:19.790
Mitarashi Heaven Bomber is an
 anime character's attack, right?

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.130
Mitarashi Heaven...

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:20.750
Yeah!

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:24.510
Bomber!

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.080
All clean.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.180
Thank you!

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.350
Thank you.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.770
Mitsuru-chan, you're really 
good with children.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.890
I've got four younger siblings,
 so I'm used to it.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.520
Wow.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:43.050
Nagomu! You haven't finished cleaning up yet!

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.460
Coming.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.660
<i>I'm so glad.</i>

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.060
<i>They like it.</i>

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.910
<b>I saw you on social media and came to listen! It's so good!!

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.590
Thank you for today.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.910
Mitsuru-chan...

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:11.210
Here. The anniversary of your grandmother's 
death is coming up, isn't it?

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:15.660
She loved higashi sweets made from 
wasanbon. Go ahead and give her some.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.730
<b>Traditional Confectionery
 Ryokushou</b>

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.730
Thank you so much!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:21.820
Your grandmother was so very good to us.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:23.980
And now we've even got you 
helping us, Mitsuru-chan.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.520
Thank you.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.810
No, it's nothing.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.610
I love working here.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.500
And people really like the 
souvenirs you make for us!

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.690
We sold several more today.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.630
That makes me so happy!

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.250
I'll make some more and bring them.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:42.200
I'm using my favorite one here.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.760
I like that.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.760
I wish I had one. A chestnut manju.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.880
Oh, speaking of which...

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.360
This is you, isn't it, Nagomu-san?

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.180
Th-This is...

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:57.880
This is definitely from that time we 
were selling in front of the station!

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.260
When did they take that?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.930
You're the one who went to get 
your picture taken, aren't you?

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.120
Wh-What is it?

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:05.730
Nothing!

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.890
It's nothing. Nothing at all...

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.170
Mitsuru-chan is in her second 
year of high school, right?

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.680
Isn't it hard for her to 
work part-time every day?

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.960
She said she wants to take care 
of her university tuition herself.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.880
She really is so responsible.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:27.660
And she must be such a help to her parents.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.640
She even helps Itsuka with 
her studies sometimes.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.030
Such a good young lady.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:34.970
Yes.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:38.300
I can help with studying, too!

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.480
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.480
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.480
Okay! I guess I won't!

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:51.240
<i>I'm so glad. I managed to make it to 
the discount sale at the supermarket.</i>

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.490
I'm home!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.060
Hey, Big Sis, welcome home!

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.240
Welcome home!

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.440
'Come home!

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.700
Welcome home.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.200
Here.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.780
You went grocery shopping for me?

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:08.020
Milk and yogurt were on sale.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:18.810
Grandpa, Grandma, these are 
from your beloved Ryokushou.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:21.910
They look like wisteria blossoms.
 They're so pretty!

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:31.870
<i>Higashi sweets made of wasanbon, you see...</i>

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:36.310
They just crumble and melt away 
in your mouth, don't they?

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:38.660
That's what I like about them.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.410
And they aren't too sweet. 
I could eat so many of them.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:50.170
You see? Even as I said it, 
it's already disappeared.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:55.180
If I work at Ryokushou, couldn't you
 eat as much as you wanted?

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:59.930
<b>Traditional Confectionery
 Ryokushou</b>

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.930
Oh, what a sneaky way of thinking. 
Who do you take after?

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.680
Don't you worry about that.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:06.060
<i>You should go do what you love to do.</i>

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.190
What I love to do...

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:17.550
Big Brother hit me!

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.460
I knocked into you a little is all.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:24.280
Weren't you all just laughing 
and playing together?

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.050
But he...

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:25.830
Shut up!

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:31.390
Oh, dear. I can't give nice 
things to children who fight.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:32.760
Huh? What is it?

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:33.690
What is it?

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.550
Grandpa and Grandma are 
done with these, so...

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.720
These are those sugar candies!

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.310
I love these!

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.890
We haven't had dinner yet, 
so just one each, okay?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.160
It melted!

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:50.040
It's so good!

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.190
It's so sweet!

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:54.200
One more! One more!

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:53.820
No.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.080
I said just one, didn't I?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.610
You can have more tomorrow.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:58.660
Aw...

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.530
In that case, sing us something 
when we go to sleep!

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.820
I like your singing voice, Big Sis!

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.180
All right.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.700
Will I be able to say it right?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:19.320
Will I be able to tell you?

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:24.260
Honest words would be the best, but...

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.910
Welcome home.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:35.900
Thanks.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.030
Are all the kids asleep?

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.820
Mitsuru's put them to bed for me.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:43.120
I see.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:47.500
I rely on her for everything. 
She's so responsible.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.260
Yes, she is.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:52.000
She'll keep going like this, find a good job...

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.040
Eventually find a good partner...

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:57.050
And make herself a happy family. 
That's what I hope, anyway.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.810
<i>After Grandpa and Grandma died...</i>

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:12.520
<i>I wanted to help my parents, 
who were both working,</i>

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.280
<i>so I helped around the house...</i>

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.520
<i>looked after my little brothers...</i>

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.870
<i>and tried not to ask for anything 
for myself or to cause any trouble.</i>

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:23.700
<i>I know.</i>

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:29.420
<i>Just a little more... I want to 
do what I love just a little more.</i>

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.270
<i>Will I be able to say it right?</i>

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:41.560
Wow. She gets some good sound out of that.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:44.000
<i>Will I be able to tell you?</i>

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:43.690
She seems like she's still in high school.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:45.980
Um, the bath is free if...

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:49.440
<i>Honest words would be the best, but...</i>

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.110
What are you doing?

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.350
The bath is free if you want it.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:56.110
<i>If I wrote it in the sky</i>

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.480
What? Thank you!

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.780
I was told to tell you, so I did.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:00.570
<i>would you smile?</i>

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.380
Guitar?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:05.240
Oh, this? It's a video of an 
amateur giving a performance.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:06.330
<i>Even though there's nothing good about me</i>

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:08.860
It's a good song. And it seems 
like she's got quite a few fans.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:12.410
<i>The stray cat I saw earlier</i>

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:13.300
What's wrong?

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:16.510
<i>I think it was crying at the bus stop</i>

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.420
I was just thinking it's been 
a while since I heard a guitar.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:21.520
I played it just the other day 
when we were selling manju.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:22.970
That's different.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.810
It didn't work for you, huh?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.450
<i>That's the feeling I got</i>

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.960
Huh? This is Mitsuru-chan.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:29.220
<i>But it isn't enough yet...</i>

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:29.220
What?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:33.050
<i>to make me bloom in many layers</i>

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:30.720
This.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.810
It's Mitsuru-chan's phone strap.

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:36.880
<i>So I'll just sing</i>

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.520
Look! In the comments.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:42.030
<i>The chord doesn't matter</i>

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:42.030
<b>I bought a strap like that one at Ryokushou

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:41.370
Seriously?

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:47.530
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:47.530
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:47.530
What?

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:51.260
We have no one by that name here!

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.000
Oh, this is so perplexing.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.920
What is all this? We've had several 
calls like that since this morning.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.650
Just take the phone off the hook for a while!

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:03.600
We can't do that. What will 
we do if a customer calls?

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.460
There's another one.

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.660
Welcome!

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:08.760
Welcome!

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:12.760
Oh, Mitsuru-chan. You're early today.
 Is something wrong?

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.120
That's what I said! There is
 no one named Neon here!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.770
<b>Neon-chan, I tried calling!

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:21.860
It can't be...

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:24.780
<b><u>Please stop</u></b>

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:28.030
<b>Stop phone-blitzing
It's a nuisance

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.520
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:30.660
<i>How'd this happen?</i>

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:33.210
<i>I was so careful!</i>

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.750
<i>If Mom and the others find out...</i>

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:39.020
<i>They'll be so disappointed in me.</i>

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:43.960
Mitsuru-chan!

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:45.880
Itsuka-chan...

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.480
So it really was you, Mitsuru-chan?

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.020
Yes.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.860
You've been playing music, then?
 When did you start?

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.640
In middle school.

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:05.990
A friend started playing guitar, 
and she let me play, too.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.950
I just plucked the strings a little...

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:15.180
And I felt like my heart began to unfurl.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.830
I always hold myself back, but...

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:24.280
I felt like, through music, I'd be 
able to express all kinds of emotions.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.090
My friend stopped playing.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:32.170
But a year ago, I bought myself 
a guitar with the money I'd earned.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.230
I wrote some music.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:37.630
And once I did, I wanted someone to hear it.

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:43.340
I recorded myself in secret 
at a karaoke place...

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.040
Uploaded it to the internet...

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:50.990
And when I got likes and comments,
 it started being fun.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:54.120
Oh, yeah. I get it. I do.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.120
But...

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:57.300
It's all over.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.120
I'll quit working here.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.230
What?

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.880
I'll quit music, too.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.830
I'm causing problems for the shop.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:10.080
I'll take down all my songs and 
make it like they never existed.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.550
You shouldn't do that!

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.050
You shouldn't give up!

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:16.440
You looked like you were having so much fun!

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:23.100
Quitting your job at our shop... 
Quitting uploading...

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.150
I can understand that.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:29.370
It's scary to have people you don't 
know messing with you, after all.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.070
But...

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.370
Why would you quit music?

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:38.210
I haven't said anything to my parents.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.450
You can't tell them?

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:44.480
They trust me because they think 
I'm diligent and responsible.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:46.840
I just can't open up and confide in them!

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:51.370
Mom and Dad are so busy. I just...

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:55.120
Th-This is no time for me 
to be doing whatever I want.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:57.910
I just feel like this 
might be the right time.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.980
This isn't what you call the "right time."

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.840
The real "right time"...

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.650
is when you've played in a band for 
ten years and never been very popular!

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.660
Your band mates leave you, 
and you realize you're all alone.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.780
And just when a big hole's 
been poked in your heart...

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:20.290
You decide to go back to your 
parents' place! That's the "right time"!

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.470
What an uncool example.

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:23.330
What?

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:31.290
If you've already decided to give up, why not
 use that courage for something else?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.090
Okay.

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:39.640
Why don't we head out for a while?

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:49.900
I beg of you! Please allow Mitsuru-chan 
to do what she wants to do!

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.110
N-N-N-Nagomu-san!

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:55.690
Wait a moment, please.

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:58.330
This conversation is all too sudden.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.870
I am ashamed to ask this of you, but...

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.780
When I said I had something 
I wanted to do and left home,

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.960
my parents didn't say anything. 
They just let me go.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:10.920
They let me do as I liked, and I'm 
truly grateful to them for that.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:14.950
In the end, I did give up that dream,

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.490
but I have no regrets 
about the decision I made.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:22.630
So, won't you give that to Mitsuru-chan, too?

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:26.090
Mitsuru-chan's music...

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:28.490
I really like it!

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:34.860
Mitsuru-chan...

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:39.280
You can do this! Say it 
like you do in your music!

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.030
Tell her your feelings!

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:44.520
Yes.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:50.120
Thank you, Itsuka-chan, Nagomu-san.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.520
Still...

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:09.520
To think you'd go barging 
into someone else's house.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.720
Huh? Was that bad?

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:17.650
But, well... It might have been 
good for Mitsuru-chan's sake.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:22.280
I hope it all turns out okay.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.420
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.420
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.090
Good morning!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.170
Morning!

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:38.920
Off to school?

00:18:38.920 --> 00:18:39.930
Yes.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:44.440
That's a pleasant smile. Were you able 
to talk with your father after that, too?

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.680
I came to give a report about that.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.660
After that, that night...

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:55.310
When I told them I want to keep playing music,

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:58.700
and I want to work in a field 
that involves music...

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.260
Honestly! Why didn't you 
say something sooner?

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.700
It makes us feel lonely!

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.700
...is what they said as they scolded me.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:09.540
After that, my whole family started 
a watch party of my videos...

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.440
What's with the mask?

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:09.050
Did you make it?

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:12.880
I experienced an impressive amount 
of pleasurable embarrassment.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.290
Man, that's rough.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:18.800
But everyone said they liked my songs!

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.350
That's really great.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:21.160
Yes!

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:25.510
I've been checking online, but...

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:30.000
It looks like everyone's gotten bored 
with hunting down your real identity.

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:31.020
<b>Neon - I tried making a new song</b>

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.020
Instead of that...

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.500
They say that my mom is funny on the phone.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:36.350
I've told you, there is no such person here!

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:38.830
More importantly, do you like wagashi?

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.780
Do you eat anko at all?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:45.200
This old lady wants young people 
to eat more wagashi, you see!

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:45.530
<b>Oak Leaf Mochi</b>

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:45.530
<b>Noblewoman's Raiment</b>

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:45.530
<b>Secret Letter</b>

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:49.350
And it seems there have been some kids 
who really did come to buy wagashi.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:50.540
<b>I subscribed to the channel

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.220
It might be good promotion for our shop.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.750
U-Um...

00:19:55.750 --> 00:20:02.090
I-I... I watched videos 
of your band, Nagomu-san!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:03.430
Huh? Really?

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:09.430
And... I like your music, too, Nagomu-san.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.410
Thank you! Makes me feel sort of embarrassed.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.320
And here...

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:17.820
While I was at it, I made a 
chestnut manju phone strap, so...

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.900
I can have it? Thank you!

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.600
Oh, right. Wait just a sec.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:33.690
Here you go.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:34.540
As a thank you.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.720
They're broken, so we can't sell them.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.290
Thank you so much!

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:45.380
Itsuka-chan! Morning!

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.920
Good morning.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:49.940
Let's go part of the way together!

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:51.510
Okay!

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.170
I'm going now!

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.600
Be careful!

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:07.590
You seem happy.

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:11.040
Oh, right.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:14.000
Shall we eat these together?

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.160
Wasanbon higashi sweets?

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:17.290
Yes.

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:23.050
Nagomu-san is a good person, isn't he?

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:27.000
He's warm-hearted and treats everyone kindly.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.550
He does... does he?

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:36.470
<i>It crumbles and melts in your mouth, right?</i>

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:41.360
<i>I really feel like I'll be able to 
write the best song I've ever written.</i>

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:46.320
<b>For Pedestrians and Cyclists</b>

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:49.470
Mitsuru-chan...

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:50.250
Hm?

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:53.960
You should probably think 
it over a little more.

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:55.660
Huh? Think about what?

00:21:56.150 --> 00:21:59.370
Well... How can I put it...

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:40.020
What is this tiny, strange little doll?

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:42.730
Huh? It's really cool, isn't it?

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:45.040
Let's make it the Ryokushou mascot!

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:46.180
Never!

00:23:50.030 --> 00:24:10.050
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:24:10.050
<b>"A Summer Night's Accompaniment"</b>

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:57.030
I like European sweets.

00:23:57.030 --> 00:23:58.120
Bye-bye.

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:01.040
I got turned down.

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:06.340
Itsuka-chan's father is missing, isn't he?

00:24:06.340 --> 00:24:07.960
I learned how to hypnotize people.

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:09.130
Papa?!
